window.docContents[142].resolve({"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Worked-Examples/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Worked-Examples--Ex-Falso-Quodlibet":{"contents":"From a proof of the absurdity, ⊥ elimination proves any proposition.\n\n   [⊥]\n  ──────  ⊥E\n    P\n  ────────  →I\n   ⊥ → P\n\n\nexample (P : Prop) : False → P :=\n  fun h => False.elim h\n\n\nexample (P : Prop) : False → P := by\n  intro h\n  exact False.elim h\n\n\n","context":"Formal Software Verification\u0009Lecture 1: Motivation and Propositional Logic\u0009Worked Examples","header":"1.8.2. Ex Falso Quodlibet","id":"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Worked-Examples/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Worked-Examples--Ex-Falso-Quodlibet"}});